ions\n\n3.6.1\n\n### System information\n\nMX Linux, 3.6.1\n\n### Issue description\n\nHey everyone,\n\nmaybe I'm doing something stupid but Godot tells me an external directory doesn't exist even though I'm accessing files in it.\n\nThis is my code:\n\n```\nextends Node2D\n\nvar dir_save_path = \"res://a\"\nvar dir = Directory.new()\n\nvar file_save_path = \"res://a/yes.txt\"\nvar file = File.new()\n\n\nfunc _ready():\n\n\tdir.open(dir_save_path)\n\tdir.dir_exists(dir_save_path)\n\tprint(dir.dir_exists(dir_save_path))\n\n\tfile.open(\"res://a/yes.txt\", File.READ)\n\tprint(file.get_csv_line())\n```\n\nI get always a false for the dir_exists but can read the file. The game is exported in debug, there is a folder called \"a\" in the same directory with a file called \"yes.txt\" with yes being the only content.\n\nThe game returns:\nFalse\n[yes]\n\nThe same happened if I wrote user instead of res\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nSee above\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nSee above","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111605/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111605/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}